  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "techno: a driving kick on every beat, an open hat on every offbeat (where a record has the ride), closed sixteenths, a clap on two and four, and a rolling sub on the sixteenths after each kick",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "One bar. The ride of a Berlin or Detroit record is an open hat here: the ride is registered and weighs nought on the offbeat lane. The sub rolls — the second and fourth sixteenth of each beat, the kick's own sixteenth left to the kick — which is the rumble a techno low end moves on."
  }
